⚡️🇺🇸 Anduril Industries delivered the first ‘Fury’ Collaborative Combat Aircraft (CCA) to the USAF on 24 September, 2026.

The Fury CCA is roughly the same size as it’s manned counterparts and will perform roles such as sensor support, close-in defense, and is meant to be a more-disposable weapon compared to manned aircrafts, with USAF testing having proved that American 5th Generation stealth fighters can control as many as a dozen (12) CCAs in simulations, and the F-15 Strike Eagle & Eagle II being capable of controlling and operating as much as two dozen (24) in simulations. While these aren’t exactly capable of being fully translated into reality, the Collaborative Combat Aircraft/Loyal Wingman design could be bringing in a whole new era of aerial dominance for whoever figures it all out first.

